  "id": "COMPOUND:30125 - PROTEIN:2272",
  "verbalization": "Luteolinidin 3-O-glucoside appears to interact with the Type-2 angiotensin II receptor, which serves as a common target for multiple compounds, including Sinigrin potassium, Thalifendine, and Npc167932. These compounds all lead to the Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28, suggesting a potential pathway where Luteolinidin 3-O-glucoside may modulate the activity of the Type-2 angiotensin II receptor, thereby influencing the downstream function of Disintegrin and metalloproteinase domain-containing protein 28. The shared target of these compounds implies a possible mechanism of action involving the angiotensin II receptor, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a functional link between Luteolinidin 3-O-glucoside and the target protein, but further investigation is needed to clarify the specific molecular mechanism.",
